0..74 Comment "/// This source converts two cases over cases of one stuck recursive call."
75..78 Comment "///"
79..211 Comment "/// It pins how the checker compares `outer(first(look(a, b)))` with the same cases, each written again by a twin of its definition."
212..215 Comment "///"
216..568 Comment "/// Each side\'s outer case eliminates a held endpoint whose computation is itself a case over the held call `look(a, b)`. The kernel reads each side as binds stacked over that call and makes them one by associativity. The checker records those steps, then compares the calls and the cases over one fresh variable, and the kernel replays the comparison."
569..572 Comment "///"
573..589 Comment "/// - see: #3086"
590..605 Comment "/// - see: #879"
